  "claims": [
    {
      "id": "claim_afa817b7af4a4dbbb5b1708e27d18a3f",
      "statement": "The `keys` table (defined in `lib/db/schema.ts` and materialized in migration `0010_concerned_exodus.sql`) stores one encrypted API key per user per provider; the unique index `keys_user_id_provider_idx` enforces one row per `(user_id, provider)` pair, the provider column is a five-value text enum (`anthropic | openai | cursor | gemini | aigateway`), and the `value` column is the AES-256-CBC ciphertext of the plaintext key produced by `lib/crypto.ts:encrypt`.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://lib/db/migrations/0010_concerned_exodus.sql#L15-L22",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:6824b791fb7f73472d3f3773748faed158771a17bc307d32b39f1abcc9d9fe3c:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://lib/db/schema.ts#L318-L336",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:81926c03f39aa8d81fe10e6018ec50618fd4ac567b84ba11c421d8a2c5bf5b50:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_05a4271012174f8b8faa0ce11695b4f0",
      "statement": "`/api/api-keys` exposes GET/POST/DELETE; all three require a signed-in session (returning `401 Unauthorized` otherwise), POST is the only handler that calls `encrypt(...)`, and none of the three ever return a decrypted `value` to the client — GET returns only `(provider, createdAt)` pairs.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://app/api/api-keys/route.ts#L11-L113",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:01d7cc5c3d50139cdcb643f57c2aac6e827f18403effa51875f63b2c46cb055c:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_ed96d82149f34307903681199310183d",
      "statement": "POST `/api/api-keys` implements the upsert as a JavaScript-level read-then-update-or-insert (not a single SQL `ON CONFLICT` statement) and assigns a fresh `nanoid()` to the `id` column only on insert; the dialog's loading-state disable is what closes the race window in practice.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://app/api/api-keys/route.ts#L57-L82",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:1be186d67e53dd8cceda2b4daaf72dbd9c9c988b4c05f10f01dbce0998086b95:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://components/api-keys-dialog.tsx#L75-L107",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:4d8e71d9526f1fd40832ad1766d22cf2a3af134dad75ad87c5f822224eab346d:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_d63753155eeb4182a5f390516f15bdfa",
      "statement": "`GET /api/api-keys/check?agent=…&model=…` is unauthenticated (no `getSessionFromReq` call); it always calls `getUserApiKey(provider)`, which itself falls back to `process.env.*` when there is no session, so an anonymous caller sees the system-env reachability for the requested agent/model combination.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://app/api/api-keys/check/route.ts#L37-L92",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:0a296e23616e6c19cbfd2c3ebe71a41c6b05c400844bdefd147c07354b7e80e7:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://lib/api-keys/user-keys.ts#L73-L103",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:6f8da8cdebb5f6c7bf9e4a3fdc5c30925b74e7c053e43c1148ae3d99c74d4d64:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_f3b7c54005984bbabbf45cd17a6e0ca2",
      "statement": "/api/api-keys/check encodes a fixed agent-to-provider default map (`claude → aigateway`, `codex → aigateway`, `cursor → cursor`, `gemini → gemini`, `opencode → openai`) and a model-name override for cursor/opencode that switches the resolved provider to `anthropic` when the lowercase model contains `claude`/`sonnet`/`opus`, to `gemini` when it contains `gemini`, and to `aigateway` when it contains `gpt`/`openai`; copilot is special-cased to read the GitHub token and reports `provider: 'github'`.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://app/api/api-keys/check/route.ts#L7-L77",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:6f9971a395afb62aa29535018aaea3f7ec9a8653aec25a704c9a3807ba9590d0:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_7a602602a6284ed2b61864a00aa72016",
      "statement": "`getUserApiKeys()` and `getUserApiKey(provider)` implement a three-step precedence: initialize the result object from `process.env.*`; if there is a session, select all matching `keys` rows, `decrypt` each `value`, and overwrite the matching provider field; any DB or decryption error is caught, logged with `console.error('Error fetching user API keys', error)`, and the function returns the env-initialized object — a user key therefore always wins over the system env for the provider it is set on, and partial user configuration (some providers overridden, others not) is the default.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://lib/api-keys/user-keys.ts#L15-L103",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:a5119d2117f1392d26e4e32caa1118fcfb88cffeb09e76781636180458c53718:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_4ac1d6a182d94c909e604043a44018d0",
      "statement": "`executeAgentInSandbox` in `lib/sandbox/agents/index.ts` snapshots the original `process.env.*` values for all five provider keys plus `GH_TOKEN`/`GITHUB_TOKEN`, assigns the user-supplied values from the `apiKeys` argument onto `process.env` for the duration of the per-agent `try` block, and always restores the snapshot in a `finally` block — this is what lets per-agent wrappers (`lib/sandbox/agents/{claude,codex,cursor,gemini,opencode}.ts`) read `process.env.*` directly without accepting the key as a parameter.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://lib/sandbox/agents/index.ts#L149-L158",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:d3c69f6a9bb5cd8ad4a923b4a9911624a2ded3cc79c662918ff5a384d13cac8b:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://lib/sandbox/agents/index.ts#L57-L75",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:72817eae14977954c546e5693850d51e1173b7efbccb171e6852761ed0e8104f:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_9729b30dba824cd996842dcbb2786693",
      "statement": "The task creation and continuation routes (`app/api/tasks/route.ts`, `app/api/tasks/[taskId]/continue/route.ts`) call `getUserApiKeys()` *before* entering the Next.js `after(...)` callback and thread the resulting object through `processTaskWithTimeout` → `processTask` → `createSandbox` → `executeAgentInSandbox`, because `getServerSession()` inside `after` can race with the request lifecycle and return `undefined` — the user keys therefore persist across the `after` boundary as a plain parameter rather than being re-resolved on the worker path.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://app/api/tasks/%5BtaskId%5D/continue/route.ts#L87-L115",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:bcec3171a805a0561f95a5ca79a3342f23ef9fafd88501d88e6c20bff84d7bb7:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://app/api/tasks/route.ts#L213-L243",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:fdd0e3f10e12f2d58226d788cf01c2f6bfae27b5e042e07b52c9a354a06c7e51:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_8b9f6de49846421bb4fa734f899484ce",
      "statement": "The five DB-side provider enum values (`anthropic`, `openai`, `cursor`, `gemini`, `aigateway`) map to the seven env vars that the agent CLIs actually read (`ANTHROPIC_API_KEY`, `OPENAI_API_KEY`, `CURSOR_API_KEY`, `GEMINI_API_KEY`, `AI_GATEWAY_API_KEY`); `AI_GATEWAY_API_KEY` drives both the Claude and Codex wrappers (and is also accepted by opencode as a fallback to `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY`), and Copilot is the one agent whose credential does not flow through this table at all — it reads `process.env.GH_TOKEN`/`GITHUB_TOKEN` from `getUserGitHubToken()`.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://lib/sandbox/agents/claude.ts#L87-L178",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:1ca5926eb58ce6a89ebb8353dd1b98d40de3c845ff40acb99f236ac411235c49:"
        },
        {
